    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠσιολογ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>discourse on nature, investigate natural causes and
				phenomena,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. περὶ πάντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					988b27
				</span></i>
			, cf. Polystr.<i><span class="en">
				p.12
			</span></i> W., <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.921d
			</span></i>, al.: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθῶς φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					2.42
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.118d
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Oen.
				3
			</span></i>: c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἰχθῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Gym.</u>
					44
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>explain from natural principles,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τιμαῖος φ. τὴν ψυχὴν κινεῖν τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>de An.</u>
					406b26
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.506
			</span></i>.</div>
